apple-bridge's fix for icloud-md 0.6.2: uniform paragraph styles.

Apple's text system takes a paragraph's style from its first character;
icloud-md reads it (and verifies its pushes) from the paragraph's newline.
Text a push inserts at a paragraph boundary inherits the neighbouring
paragraph's attribute run, and the reconciler only corrected the fields the
newline said were wrong, so typing at the start of a checklist item or
heading, or retyping a line next to a table, could upload a paragraph that is
one thing to icloud-md and another to the iPhone. Such a note passed
icloud-md's verification and made Notes on the iPhone hang.

This patch makes the reconciler rewrite any paragraph whose characters
disagree, starting every piece from the paragraph's own style, and makes push
refuse to upload (or create) a note that still has one. install.sh applies it
with `patch -p1` in the package directory; tests/test_icloud_md_patch.py
checks it.

