+ * apple-bridge patch: uniform paragraph styles.
+ *
+ * Apple's text system takes a paragraph's style from its first character;
+ * this tool's decoder (and so its push verification) reads it from the
+ * paragraph's newline. The two agree only when every character of the
+ * paragraph carries the same paragraphStyle. A splice can break that: text
+ * inserted at a paragraph boundary inherits the neighbouring paragraph's run
+ * (`adjustAttributeRuns`), and the overlay below only fixed the fields the
+ * newline's projection said were wrong. The result - say a checklist line
+ * whose characters are Body with one todo uuid while its newline is a
+ * checklist with another - passes verification here and leaves Notes on the
+ * iPhone unresponsive.
